<article class="env-lemma" id="0H7S">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0H7S">Lemma <span data-tag="0H7S">15.43.3</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : R \to S$ be a ring map. Assume </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
$\varphi $ is regular, 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$S$ is Noetherian, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
$R$ is Noetherian and regular. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $S$ is regular. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      For Noetherian rings being regular is the same as having properties $(R_ k)$ for all $k$. Hence we may apply Algebra, Lemma <a href="/tag/033A" data-tag="033A">10.163.5</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>